# Add Changenote (`About/changelog.txt`)

Mlie's **Add Changenote** replaces Steam's `[Auto-generated text]` on in-game Workshop upload. It only copies the block whose **first line starts with the current `modVersion`**. A `[h1]` heading first = skipped = you paste by hand.

## Required

1. Read `About.xml` `modVersion` (not the build stamp, not RimWorld 1.6).
2. Current-version block: first non-`#` line **starts with that exact number**, then a newline, then Steam BBCode.
3. Steam paste = **this version only**. Older `x.y.z` blocks may sit below; the next version-number line ends the extract.
4. `#` lines are ignored. No `Manifest.xml` unless asked — version comes from `modVersion`.
5. File lives at `About/changelog.txt` in the folder that gets uploaded.

## Do

```
# Deep Colony — ignored

1.5.2
[h1]Deep Colony — 1.5.2[/h1]

[b]Fixed[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]Last of the line[/b] — only when the last living colony blood kin dies.
[/list]

[i]Build stamp (Player.log): last-of-line-v1[/i]
```

## Do not

```
[h1]Deep Colony — 1.5.2[/h1]
```

```
1.5.2 Last of the line
```

(That second form works for Add Changenote but drops BBCode. Prefer version-on-its-own-line, then `[h1]`.)
